Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-22-2001||01:59 AM||||If you just want to change the color of the plastic/vinyl...go to a auto body shop and look through interior colors.  They can get any color and spray your parts.  You can do it yourself too.  Go to a NAPA and look through the color catalogs.  This requires a professional paint gun/compressor.  This is dye not paint... and it won't rub off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ambush||08-22-2001||02:09 AM||||Don't spray it. After a few sit downs that s*** comes off. Ask them about the warranty. You will see that it's not very long. The best thing to do is go to a fabric shop, buy a whole bunch of the color vinyl, leather or cloth you want then either do it yourself or pay someone to replace or cover your old ones. (P.S.don't forget to buy glue)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||08-22-2001||08:48 AM||||Mr. Mike, I thought still made interior kits for ~$1500.  You could also go to an upholstery shop for a price on an interior overhaul.  Get a few estimates.  What I've seen these shops do nice work at an acceptable price.||||reg||1
